% Arity, every function, both edges.
%
% E_ARITY is a compile-time error raised from parseCall before a single argument
% is evaluated, so the filler arguments are deliberately meaningless — `1` parses
% and never runs. The position is the *call's*, which is why every case pins it:
% this is the cheapest cross-host position check in the suite, and there are 61
% functions behind it.
%
% Generated shape, maintained by hand. A new built-in lands with its two cases
% here in the same change; tools/check-api.sh will tell you the count moved.

### name: arity.abort.too-few
--- source
ABORT()
--- expect
error E_ARITY at 1:1
===
### name: arity.abort.too-many
--- source
ABORT(1, 1)
--- expect
error E_ARITY at 1:1
===
